# #568: via size as a query-time parameter (per-rung via legality) — UNAPPLIED PATCH (v2)
#
# v2 adds the missing Python-visible plumbing: route_multi AND route_with_frontier
# take `via_rung=0` as a trailing kwarg (backwards-compatible; default 0 =
# baseline byte-identical), threaded into SearchOptions per SEARCH — no router
# state to set/reset, so a rung retry can never leak into the next net's route.
#
# Rust core (this patch, compile-checked in a scratch tree, NOT built into the
# distributed .so — verify with build_router.py after apply):
#   obstacle_map.rs: blocked_vias_small refcount map (subset semantics; EMPTY =
#     unpopulated = rung>=1 queries fall back to blocked_vias, so single-rung
#     callers are byte-identical); add/remove single+batch mirrors; clone/init/
#     freeze covered (static bitmap blocks all rungs — conservative; freeze
#     clears the small map as redundant); is_via_blocked_rung(gx, gy, rung).
#   router.rs: SearchOptions.via_rung (default 0), route_multi/route_with_frontier
#     kwarg `via_rung=0`, consulted at the via-transition test (free-via
#     override composes unchanged).
#   Cargo.toml: 0.19.3 -> 0.20.0 (rides the already-pending 0.20.0 release).
#
# Python integration REQUIRED before this does anything (not in this patch —
# scoped 2026-08-04 with Andy: plane-script call sites are EXCLUDED, that
# routing is retired by the pours-first chain):
#   1. obstacle_cache: NetObstacleData.blocked_vias_small; builders compute the
#      via-block cell set a SECOND time at the small-rung reserve (from the
#      fab_floor_ladder smallest (diameter, drill) PAIR: dia/2 + clearance +
#      track/2, drill h2h from the drill) and add/remove_net_obstacles_from_cache
#      stamp/remove both maps.
#   2. run_obstacle_audit: Rust get_stats now emits blocked_vias_small as the
#      8th element (appended LAST; all Python consumers are index-based, none
#      unpack a fixed arity -- verified obstacle_map.py/_ledger,
#      memory_debug.py stats[:6], test_obstacle_addremove_parity indexing).
#      Python side: append "blocked_vias_small" to the audit labels tuple AND
#      the HARD set in run_obstacle_audit, so a small-map leak fails the same
#      working==base+caches gate as blocked_vias.
#      RUN the balance gates after integration (they are the acceptance bar
#      for touching the core map, per Andy):
#        - tests/test_obstacle_map_balance.py  (standing gate)
#        - a chain board with KICAD_OBSTACLE_AUDIT=1 -> "BALANCED" incl. the
#          new label, and KICAD_OBSTACLE_LEDGER=1 for per-serial attribution
#          if it is not.
#   3. _via_rung_retry: replace the free-via overlay + bbox sampling + exact
#      site validator with a plain re-search passing via_rung=1; register the
#      small (dia, drill) in pcb_data._unblock_via_sizes for each via cell of
#      the returned path (#339 emission re-validates and shrink-to-fits).
#   4. #189 boxed-pad unblock retry: try a via_rung=1 re-search BEFORE
#      pre-placing a ladder via; pre-placement stays as final fallback only
#      (via-in-pad still needs the free-via override).
#   5. net_rescue._escalation_rungs: collapse the per-via-size config rebuilds
#      to ONE window build stamping both maps + a via_rung=1 retry; per-site
#      emitted size still chosen by the #339 shrink (search at the smallest
#      rung for reachability, emit the largest that clears).
#   6. #339/_emit_via_size stays as the emission-time assert/shrink — no longer
#      the legality-discovery mechanism once both maps stamp the same geometry.
#   7. README.md version history: 0.20.0 — per-rung via legality (#568).
#
